  "recipeCuisine": "Spain",
  "name": "Paella",
  "text": "Paella\n\nYield: 6-8\n\nIngredients\n\n60 g chorizo (cut into thin slices),\n\n40g pancetta (finely diced),\n\n1 clove garlic (finely chopped),\n\n1/2 Spanish onion (finely diced),\n\n1/2 red pepper (diced),\n\n1/2 tsp soft thyme leaves,\n\n¼ tsp dried red chilli flakes\n\n200 g calasparra (Spanish short-grain) rice,\n\n1/2 tsp smoked paprika,\n\n75 ml oz dry white wine,\n\n400 ml chicken stock (heated with ¼ tsp saffron threads),\n\n2 boneless chicken thighs(halved and browned),\n\n6 small clams, cleaned\n\n30 g fresh or frozen peas\n\n2 medium tomatoes (de-seeded and diced),\n\nolive oil,\n\n4 garlic cloves (peeled and lightly crushed),\n\n4 jumbo raw prawns, in shells,\n\n100 g squid, cleaned and chopped into bite-sized pieces,\n\n2 tbsp chopped flat-leaf parsley,\n\nSalt and freshly ground black pepper\n\nLemon wedges.\n\nPreparation method\n\n1. Heat half the olive oil in a paella dish or heavy-based saucepan.\n\n2. Brown the chicken thighs and set aside.\n\n3. Add the chorizo and pancetta and fry until crisp.\n\n4. Add the garlic, onion and pepper and heat until softened.\n\n5. Add the thyme, chilli flakes and calasparra rice, and stir until all the grains of rice are nicely coated and glossy.\n\n6. Now add the paprika and dry white wine and when it is bubbling, pour in the hot chicken stock, add the chicken thighs and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n\n7. Now place the clams into the dish with the join facing down so that the edges open outwards. Sprinkle in the peas and chopped tomatoes and continue to cook gently for another 10 minutes.\n\n8. Meanwhile, heat the remaining oil with the garlic cloves in a separate pan and add the prawns. Fry quickly for a minute or two then add them to the paella. Now do the same with the squid and add them to the paella too.\n\n9. Scatter the chopped parsley over the paella and serve immediately.",
  "recipeYield": "6-8",
